# Normal text-file line-ending normalization for everything...
* text=auto

# ...but Go source is always LF, even in a Windows checkout with
# core.autocrlf=true: gofmt reports CRLF files as unformatted, so the Windows
# CI leg would otherwise fail "gofmt -l ." on a correct tree.
*.go text eol=lf
go.mod text eol=lf
go.sum text eol=lf

# ...except testdata directories: these are byte-exact captures (real
# /proc/<pid>/limits output, including the kernel trailing padding spaces)
# and hand-crafted fixtures whose exact bytes -- including a deliberate CRLF
# fixture -- ARE the test subject. Git must never rewrite their line endings
# on checkout/checkin (core.autocrlf=true would otherwise LF->CRLF them on a
# Windows clone, silently changing byte counts and neutering the
# CRLF-tolerance test, which would then pass vacuously because the fixture
# no longer has any CRs to tolerate).
**/testdata/** -text
